This repository is an unofficial, community port of Google's "Endpoint
Verification" browser extension (internal name: "SecureConnect") to Firefox.
It is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Google LLC or
Mozilla.

Provenance
----------
The extension logic in this repository (background_service_worker.js,
popup_script.js, options_script.js, log_script.js, offscreen_script.js,
mdl_all_js_compiled.js, and the HTML/CSS files) is the *compiled, minified
output* of Google's Chrome extension "Endpoint Verification", version
1.140.0 (Chrome Web Store item ID
callobklhcbilhphinckomhgkigmfocg), repackaged to run on Firefox. It is not
source code and cannot be meaningfully reviewed line by line. See
README.md ("Verification") for the CRX checksum, download procedure, and
the exact list of intentional differences between this package and the
official CRX. The compiled files were verified byte-identical to the
official CRX at the time of packaging.

Port-specific code added by the maintainers:
  - compat_shim.js           Chrome MV3 -> Firefox MV2 API compatibility shim
  - setup-native-host.sh     Installs Google's native helper for Firefox
  - manifest.json            Converted to Manifest V2 for Firefox

